. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * We consider a model using two-stage least squares
. 
.         * As a good proxy of support for gender equality (hypothesis 1), we a
> ssume that statements regarding attitudes or values toward women allow to cap
> ture 
.         * this dimension (variables plj0620, plj0621, plj0622, plj0623, plj06
> 24, plj0625). More precisely, we recode variables as indicating support for g
> ender equality with dummies equal to one when 
.         * respondents clearly indicate a positive opinion on a statement. The
>  final index (sprogend) is the sum of these binary indicators, which ranges f
> rom 0 to 6.
.         * We want to investigate the differential effect between males and fe
> males of having daughters on the support of gender equality.
.         * Accordingly, we run a regression analysis where we instrument the i
> nteraction between being a male and "having at least one daughter" with an in
> teraction of being a male with a dummy equal to one if the first born was a d
> augher,
.         * and we use "sprogend" as dependent variable.
. 
. ivregress 2sls sprogend ( d_daughter interaction = daughterFB interactioniv) 
> male sumkids age age2 agefb agefb2 sumkids_mv age_mv age2_mv agefb_mv agefb2_
> mv, robust
note: sumkids_mv omitted because of collinearity.
note: age_mv omitted because of collinearity.
note: age2_mv omitted because of collinearity.
